nu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-product menu-item-11815"><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/pte-exam-question-bank/">PTE Preparation Material</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-product menu-item-8926"><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/ptematerial/">PTE Real Exam Question Bank</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-product menu-item-3010"><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/pteprediction/">PTE Exam Prediction</a></li><li class="menu-item menu-item-type-custom menu-item-object-custom menu-item-2805"><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/my-account/">My Account</a></li><li class="woo-menu-icon wcmenucart-toggle-drop_down spacious toggle-cart-widget"> <a href="https://www.ptebank.com/cart/" class="wcmenucart"> <span class="wcmenucart-count"><i class=" icon-handbag" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i><span class="wcmenucart-details count">0</span></span> </a><div class="current-shop-items-dropdown owp-mini-cart clr"><div class="current-shop-items-inner clr"><div class="widget woocommerce widget_shopping_cart"><div class="widget_shopping_cart_content"></div></div></div></div></li></ul><div id="mobile-menu-search" class="clr"><form aria-label="Search this website" method="get" action="https://www.ptebank.com/" class="mobile-searchform" role="search"> <span class="screen-reader-text"> Search this website </span> <input type="search" id="ocean-mobile-search-1" class="field" name="s" autocomplete="off" value="" placeholder="Search" aria-label="Insert search query" /> <button aria-label="Submit search" type="submit" class="searchform-submit"> <i class=" icon-magnifier" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i> </button></form></div></nav></div></div></div></header><main id="main" class="site-main clr"  role="main"><header class="page-header hide-tablet-mobile"><div class="container clr page-header-inner"><h1 class="page-header-title clr" itemprop="headline">PTE Summarize Spoken Text (PTE SST February 2023)</h1></div></header><div id="content-wrap" class="container clr"><div id="primary" class="content-area clr"><div id="content" class="site-content clr"><article id="post-10478"><ul class="meta ospm-default clr"><li class="meta-cat"><span class="screen-reader-text">Post category:</span><i class=" icon-folder" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/category/exam-tips/" rel="category tag">Exam Tips</a> <span class="owp-sep">/</span> <a href="https://www.ptebank.com/category/sst/" rel="category tag">Summarize Spoken Text</a></li><li class="meta-rt"><span class="screen-reader-text">Reading time:</span><i class=" icon-cup" aria-hidden="true" role="img"></i>8 mins read</li></ul><div class="entry-content clr" itemprop="text"><h1>PTE Listening Summarize Spoken Text (SST) exam questions</h1><p>Tip: Summarize Spoken Text questions tend to have higher repeated rate than other question types in PTE Academic test. Make sure you memorise words as much as you can. We selected some of PTE predicted Summarize Spoken Text (Listening) for February 2023. You can get full version of this material by accessing <strong><span style="color: #3366ff;"><a style="color: #3366ff;" href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/pteprediction/">PTE Predicted Questions for February 2023</a></span></strong>.</p><figure id="attachment_10485" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-10485" style="width: 1024px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" class="wp-image-10485 size-large" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-1024x791.jpg" alt="Summarize Spoken Text" width="1024" height="791" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-1024x791.jpg 1024w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-scaled-600x464.jpg 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-768x593.jpg 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-1536x1187.jpg 1536w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Promotion-6-2048x1583.jpg 2048w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-10485" class="wp-caption-text">Summarize Spoken Text</figcaption></figure><p class="p1"> </p><p></p><p></p><h2>5.<b>Genes</b> | PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST)</h2> <audio class="wp-audio-shortcode" id="audio-10478-1" preload="none" style="width: 100%;" controls="controls"><source type="audio/mpeg" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Genes.mp3?_=1" /><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Genes.mp3">https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/Genes.mp3</a></audio><p class="p1">Since the discovery of DNA structure, people have believed that genes have an impact only on people’s physical structure.</p><p class="p1">However, the study of mapping of genes in 2001 found that there is a genetic responsibility to human’s physical and psychological behaviors, which has changed the way we understand our behaviors.</p><p class="p1">Findings from behavioural genetic research have broadly impacted modern understanding of the role of genetic and environmental influences on behaviour.</p><p class="p1">The research on genes has provided integrating information, and the findings can benefit biologists, psychologists and neuroscientists.</p><p class="p1">Qualitative research has fostered arguments that behavioural genetics is an ungovernable field without scientific norms or consensus, which fosters controversy.</p><p><b>Genes| PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST) &#8211; Sample Answer:</b></p><p class="p1">Since the discovery of DNA structure, people have believed that genes have an impact only on people’s physical structure. However, the study of mapping of genes in 2001 found that there is a genetic responsibility to human’s physical and psychological behaviours. <span class="Apple-converted-space">  </span>This findings have impacted modern understanding of the role of genetic and environmental influences on behaviour, which can benefit biologists, psychologists and neuroscientists. (64 words)</p><p> </p><p></p><p></p><h2>6.<b>Abstraction (Sign Language)</b> | PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST)</h2> <audio class="wp-audio-shortcode" id="audio-10478-2" preload="none" style="width: 100%;" controls="controls"><source type="audio/mpeg" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Abstraction-Sign-Language.mp3?_=2" /><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Abstraction-Sign-Language.mp3">https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/Abstraction-Sign-Language.mp3</a></audio><p> </p><p class="p2">So the topic for today is abstraction. And this is a very important layer of computer because you can&#8217;t do anything with a computer unless you have a symbolic system in place. Right. So we&#8217;re talking about the origin of symbolic systems. Language is a classic symbolic system. Apparently one theory for why language evolved is that people communicated with sign language and with movement quite well for a long time. And it turned out that they wanted to communicate even while they were doing things. So, while they were trying to strangle the dinosaur, not the dinosaurs, the rhinoceros, they wanted to say &#8220;Come help me&#8221; and they use sign language to do it. They had to let go of the rhinoceros and the rhinoceros ran away. So you can see that it&#8217;s a good idea to be able to do something with your hands and be able to communicate at the same time. Hence there come words and language</p><p class="p1">The research on genes has provided integrating information, and the findings can benefit biologists, psychologists and neuroscientists.</p><p class="p1">Qualitative research has fostered arguments that behavioural genetics is an ungovernable field without scientific norms or consensus, which fosters controversy.</p><p><b>Abstraction | PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST) &#8211; Sample Answer:</b></p><p class="p1">The abstraction which also known as description has two methods which are symbolic language and body language. Specifically, the abstraction is important for developing a computer since it originated from the symbolic system. It was created when people tried to communicate with each other by symbolic language. Furthermore, the other part of abstraction is the body language, the physical movement facilitates the development of sign language which became hand words. (70 words)</p><p> </p><p></p><p></p><h1>More Real PTE Questions for February 2023?</h1><p>Get start with signing up with PTE BANK!</p><p><span class="s1"><strong>Step 1: </strong><em><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/my-account/"><span class="s2"><b>Register</b></span></a></em></span><b> </b><span class="s1">an account</span></p><p><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/my-account/"><noscript><img decoding="async" class="aligncenter wp-image-4007" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register.png" alt="PTE Question Bank" width="850" height="500" srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register.png 1107w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-600x353.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-768x452.png 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-1024x602.png 1024w" sizes="(max-width: 850px) 100vw, 850px" /></noscript><img src='data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns=%22http://www.w3.org/2000/svg%22%20viewBox=%220%200%20850%20500%22%3E%3C/svg%3E' decoding="async" class="lazyload aligncenter wp-image-4007" data-src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register.png" alt="PTE Question Bank" width="850" height="500" data-srcset="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register.png 1107w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-600x353.png 600w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-768x452.png 768w, https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/07/register-1024x602.png 1024w" data-sizes="(max-width: 850px) 100vw, 850px" /></a></p><p><span class="s1"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Choose your perfect <em><strong><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/product/pteprediction/">PTE Exam Package</a> </strong></em></span></p><p class="p2"><span class="s1"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Go to &#8220;My Account&#8221;, click on &#8220;download&#8221; to get PTE preparation materials</span></p><p></p><p></p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-css-opacity" /><p> </p><p></p><p></p><hr class="wp-block-separator has-text-color has-white-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-white-background-color has-background" /><p> </p></p><p></p><h2>4.<b>Newspaper</b> | PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST)</h2> <audio class="wp-audio-shortcode" id="audio-10478-3" preload="none" style="width: 100%;" controls="controls"><source type="audio/mpeg" src="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/newspaper.mp3?_=3" /><a href="https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/newspaper.mp3">https://www.ptebank.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/06/newspaper.mp3</a></audio><p class="p1">Because of the economic model, the newspaper industry has been shrinking dramatically from the last 50 years of the 20th century in some states of America. Also as the economic model changed, newspapers increased the cash flow. However, there are still some newspaper industries losing money because of a decrease in advertising and buyers. They can&#8217;t find buyers. Only a few newspapers have positive cash flow. Over 100 newspapers with cash flow in red had no money to publish the newspaper everyday. Some of them published three days per week. Small-sized newspapers only published once a week and had to go online. Some newspapers even disappeared. The staff working in newspaper industry decreased by 30-60% or more.</p><p><b>Newspaper | PTE Summarize Spoken Text (SST) &#8211; Sample Answer:</b></p><p class="p1">The newspaper industry has been shrinking dramatically from